<header><p class="st-kicker">duchy · Balkans and Hungary</p><h1 class="st-title">Duchy of Menumorut</h1><p class="st-meta">890 CE – 904 CE (approx.) · capital Biharea</p></header>
<p class="st-teaser">Realm in the Crișana region around Biharea attributed by the Gesta Hungarorum to Menumorut, who resisted and then made peace with the Hungarians.</p>
<div class="st-body"><div class="st-text"><h2>Origins</h2><p><a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menumorut">Menumorut</a> is known only from the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta Hungarorum</a>, written around 1200. It places his duchy between the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tisza">Tisza</a>, the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/somes">Someș</a> and the Igfon forest, with its fortress at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biharea">Bihar</a> (Biharea), inhabited by <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/khazar-khaganate">Khazars</a> and other peoples, around the time of the Hungarian conquest of the 890s.</p><h2>Rule and society</h2><p>The <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta</a> says <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menumorut">Menumorut</a> refused to cede land to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/arpad">Árpád</a>, claiming the Byzantine emperor as his lord. Hungarian forces besieged <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/biharea">Bihar</a>, and he agreed to marry his daughter to Árpád's son <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zolta">Zoltán</a>. Excavations at Biharea show a fortified site of the period, but no contemporary written source confirms the ruler.</p><h2>Decline and legacy</h2><p>According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/gesta-hungarorum">Gesta</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/menumorut">Menumorut</a> died around 904 and his lands passed to <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/zolta">Zoltán</a>, joining the <a class="enc-link st-link" href="/state/principality-of-hungary">Principality of Hungary</a>. Romanian and Hungarian historians still debate whether the duchy existed as described.</p><p class="st-conf">Few sources survive for this state; details are uncertain.</p></div><aside class="st-side"><div class="st-emblem" role="img" aria-label="duchy, 890 CE – 904 CE (approx.)"><svg viewBox="0 0 100 100" aria-hidden="true"><path d="M20 74 H80 V60 H20 Z"/><path d="M20 60 Q35 46 50 60 Q65 46 80 60"/><circle cx="20" cy="54" r="3"/><circle cx="35" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="50" cy="44" r="3"/><circle cx="65" cy="48" r="3"/><circle cx="80" cy="54" r="3"/></svg><p class="st-emblem-type">duchy</p><p class="st-emblem-region">Balkans and Hungary</p><div class="st-span" aria-hidden="true"><span class="st-span-bar" style="left:77.41%;width:1.20%"></span></div><div class="st-span-axis" aria-hidden="true"><span>3000 BCE</span><span>1 CE</span><span>2000</span></div></div><dl class="st-facts"><dt>Years</dt><dd>890 CE – 904 CE (approx.)</dd><dt>Centuries</dt><dd><a href="/centuries/9th-century">9th century</a> – <a href="/centuries/10th-century">10th century</a></dd><dt>Type</dt><dd>duchy</dd><dt>Character</dt><dd>tribal</dd><dt>Capital</dt><dd>Biharea</dd><dt>Rulers</dt><dd>Menumorut</dd><dt>Today</dt><dd><a href="/countries/romania">Romania</a>, <a href="/countries/hungary">Hungary</a></dd><dt>Also</dt><dd>Menumorut's realm</dd></dl><figure class="st-locator"><a href="/atlas?year=897&amp;focus=duchy-of-menumorut" aria-label="Duchy of Menumorut on the atlas"><svg class="map map-loc" viewBox="5282 559 640 512" role="img" aria-label="Map: where Duchy of Menumorut lay"><image href="/maps/world.svg" x="0" y="0" width="10000" height="4393"/><path class="map-dot-n" d="M5437 760h0"/><path class="map-dot-halo" d="M5602 815h0"/><path class="map-dot-ap" d="M5602 815h0"/></svg></a><figcaption>Location approximate: shown in present-day Romania. <a href="/atlas?year=897&amp;focus=duchy-of-menumorut">On the atlas &rarr;</a></figcaption></figure></aside></div>

